description:
globs: *.rs
alwaysApply: false
---
Performance is very important.
Doc tests are a good idea where they make sense.
Rust tests usually go in the bottom of the file in a `tests` mod.

Import common stuff and use the inner name like:
```
use std::time::Instant;

fn foo() {
    let now = Instant::now();
}
``